 "about": "A whole game written in Lua on client controls, made with the tools of this server alone and played to its end by script on 2026-10-13: 翻牌配对, twelve cards, six pairs, a minute. One script (pr_game.lua) holds all of it: a start screen with a button, the board, the turn of a card (a tween sequence that squeezes the card flat, changes its face and opens it again), a sound for a card, a pair and a miss (game.PlayAudio2D), a bar that runs down with the time (the fill of an image whose mask is on), a count of moves and pairs in a text box, a pause button that stops the level (game.PauseLevelTime) under a dark screen with a button to go on, and the end: the script sends PR_win or PR_lose and the graph settles the level. The cards are copies of the template PR_card made by the script (the index of the template is read from a reference control, not written into the script); the faces are the six plain shapes of the picture library (100001 to 100006), tinted. In a playtest the deck is not shuffled (game.IsTestPlay()), so that a script of clicks can play it: this route presses 开始, opens two cards that do not match, pauses and goes on, then opens the six pairs. Prints: PR_LUA ready cards 12, start, paused, resumed, pair 1 to pair 6, win moves 7 left 48, and PR_VICTORY from the graph; the platform's own 胜利 screen follows. The run was given expect {prints} and answered passed. Before the first play scene_add_client_ui pointed out a mistake in the script (CONTROL_NOT_A_CHILD: GetChild(\"moves\") on the root, while moves stands under hud); with that corrected the game ran as written at the first playtest. editor_preview_interface shows the interface inside the canvas of a phone (16:9 and 4:3) and of a console. The text needs an account of 奇匠 level 2.",
 "durationSeconds": 19,
